# Livil — Cursor AI Guidelines

## What is Livil?
Livil is a social music platform — think Spotify + Discord + SoundCloud.
Users can upload music (audio + video), listen together in real time (Jam rooms), chat with friends, build shared playlists, and follow each other's listening activity.

## Cursor Behavior Rules
- Always follow the confirmed dependency versions listed below. Never suggest upgrading or downgrading without explicit instruction.
- Always use `FormInput` component for any text input — never create raw `TextInput` with lifted focus state.
- Always use `createNativeStackNavigator` — never `createStackNavigator`.
- Always keep dark theme (`#0A0A0F` background, `#7C3AED` purple accent).
- When adding new screens, follow the existing file structure under `src/screens/`.
- When adding new navigation, update `src/navigation/types.ts` with the new route params.
- Never install new packages without checking compatibility with RN 0.78.0 first.
- Always bump `versionCode` in `android/app/build.gradle` before a new Play Store release.
- Never commit `android/app/livil-release.keystore` or passwords to git.

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Mobile App | React Native 0.78.0 (no Expo) |
| Language | TypeScript |
| Navigation | @react-navigation/native-stack (v7) |
| Backend/Auth | Supabase |
| Database | Supabase PostgreSQL |
| File Storage | Cloudflare R2 (planned) |
| Real-time | Socket.io (planned) |

